loader.efi: clear dctx->zstdstrm in zstd_fini(), as xz_fini() does, so the
second decomp_fini() of do_download_ramdisk()'s error paths does not free
the ZSTD DStream again.

Tutorial: FreeBSD/docs/loader_memdisk_zstd_fini.md
Test: FreeBSD/docs/loader_memdisk_zstd_fini_test.sh
Reported by: llm-postcr, POSTCR-a2adf568cdfe83d8aca49f9eb9ba7891e88ff3cd-1
Base: main at 29b24020f6fa (2026-11-12).

diff --git a/stand/efi/loader/decompress.c b/stand/efi/loader/decompress.c
index c90634037260..704b5288123d 100644
--- a/stand/efi/loader/decompress.c
+++ b/stand/efi/loader/decompress.c
@@ -426,6 +426,7 @@ static void
 zstd_fini(decomp_state *dctx, bool flush)
 {
 	ZSTD_freeDStream(dctx->zstdstrm);
+	dctx->zstdstrm = NULL;
 	if (!flush)
 		return;
 	free_buffer(dctx);
